 "_comment": "Shared cross-SDK conformance vectors for the PRISM contract. RFC 8785 (JCS) pins THREE things and every SDK must agree on all three: (1) strings raw UTF-8, never backslash-u escaped; (2) numbers rendered per ECMAScript Number::toString (1.0 -> 1, -0.0 -> 0, fixed/exponential switch at 1e21 / 1e-7); (3) object keys sorted by UTF-16 CODE UNITS, not code points. Pinned 2026-07-29 after all three were MEASURED diverging between prism-py and prism-js. The num_* and key_sort_astral cases are exactly what a string-escaping-only fix leaves broken.",
