 "_structural_comment": "Deterministic CBOR (RFC 8949 4.2) content addresses — 'structural permanence'. Every SDK must reproduce `cbor_hex` byte-for-byte and `sha256` exactly. A {\"$bigint\": \"...\"} value must be reconstituted natively (Python int / JS BigInt) BEFORE encoding: JSON cannot carry an integer beyond 2^53, and JS JSON.parse would silently round it — which is precisely the defect structural encoding removes. Under JCS that same value COLLIDES with 9007199254740992. | 2026-07-29 (Contract Builder): added the 64-bit/bignum handover boundary (s_u64_max, s_bignum_pos, s_i64_floor, s_bignum_neg, s_bignum_wide). Before this, integers >= 2^64 raised in Python and were SILENTLY TRUNCATED to 64 bits in JS, so the two SDKs computed different addresses for the same integer with neither raising. Major type 0/1 is REQUIRED whenever the value fits in 64 bits and a bignum only beyond, or one integer would have two encodings.",
 "structural_algo": "cbor-det-sha256",
