 "_junction_comment": "THE JUNCTION vectors (added 2026-07-29, Contract Builder — NEXT.md §5.3). capability_drift.py compares capability NAMES only and 'would not have caught a single item in §5.1'. It did not: cross-checking these four functions between prism-py and prism-js found TWO live divergences in the code that decides whether a host grounds a crystal at all. (1) prism-js required only `name`, so a TS host GROUNDED crystals Python REFUSES — measured 3 problems in py vs 0 in js on the same crystal. (2) prism-py had NO capability-spelling check on organon `requires`, so PYTHON — the canonical implementation and the side that SIGNS crystals — validated a requirement no platform will honour, the exact failure prism-js's own comment describes as 'how prism-c shipped webgpu'. Each SDK held half the validation. Both fixed; problem MESSAGES are now byte-identical, which is why they are pinned verbatim rather than by count.",
